On Wed, 22 Mar 2006, Yanis Batura wrote:

> Following are my ideas which can be implemented in jboselkei.
>
> 1) Titles. For achieving certain ratings users will receive
> titles, for example, for rating 10 a user will receive title "white
> belt", for 50 - "yellow belt", ..., for 1000 - "Master", for 2500
> -"Grandmaster" etc. The question is in names and numbers for titles. I
> think titles will be an additional stimulus for people to translate
> in jboselkei.

I think the titles would definitely be best in lojban.

> 2) giving 0.1 r.p. for each post and each review so that people have
> something as reward for their work

That's probably a pretty good idea.

> 3) Computing proficiency in Lojban as: selecting only those translations
> from the set of the translations made by the user that were reviewed by at
> least three reviewers, then find an average value of these translations.
> (An value of a translation is a product of its estimated difficulty and its
> estimated quality.) This is, however, much more difficult to realize in
> real-time comparing with computing ratings themselves.

Sounds like a more meaningful (or different meaning) rating than the normal
rating.  Sounds interesting.

> What do you think about these ideas?

They sound pretty good.  However, at present my number one wish would be some
way to comment on reviews.  It seems like every day I see more reviews that
just plain aren't correct, and having no way to correct them is frustrating.
